import csv
import os
OUT=os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)),'..','..','v1_assessment.csv')
rows=[
('Years-based proficiency level labels (Foundational 0-2 y; Intermediate 3-5 y; Advanced 6-10 y; Expert 10+ y)','source text level labels (data/v1_baseline/source_text/proficiency.csv source_level_label); Proficiency Indicators sheet','retire','Tenure is a weak predictor of performance (prehire experience rho ~ .06) and a known adverse-impact and age-claim exposure when used as a threshold. It duplicates and conflicts with OPM specialized-experience rules and the push toward technical assessments under the Chance to Compete Act and the Merit Hiring Plan. It also disadvantages cross-sector movers with discontinuous careers. v1 own methodology research recommended responsibility-based levels instead. Replace with L1-L5 responsibility-anchored levels; keep years only as descriptive typical_time_to_level from survey data.','E','IO-046|IO-047|IO-048|IO-049|IO-020|IO-021|IO-030|IO-031|IO-004','IO'),
('Four levels applied to every competency','Proficiency Indicators sheet (888 rows = 222 x 4)','change','Forces levels where no such work exists (e.g., 2.5.2 Collaborative document management has an Expert level "Advances document management in environmental sector"). Adopt per-competency level spans defined only where job analysis, SME consensus and assessable indicators support them (proficiency_model_v2.md s.5).','E','IO-001|IO-004|IO-061','IO'),
('Knowledge statements (one per level)','Proficiency Indicators col Knowledge; Competencies sheet','change','85.5% scored 0 or 1 on OBS-4 in the blind sample (61% inferred states such as Understands/Familiar/Expert in; 24% reputation, e.g., Shapes). 209/222 Foundational K begin Understands/Familiar/Aware; 217/222 Advanced K begin "Expert in"; 211/222 Expert K begin "Shapes". Rewrite as testable knowledge elements (layer B), not performance statements. UGESP content validity cannot rest on inferred mental states.','E','IO-010|IO-020','IO'),
('Application statements (one per level)','Proficiency Indicators col Application','change','Only 16% directly observable; 61% need specification; 23% not individually assessable (mostly Expert: "Provides leadership", "Leads transformative"). Fold into L-level indicators with condition and standard.','E','IO-010','IO'),
('Foundational and Intermediate indicators','Proficiency Indicators cols Indicator 1-6, levels FOUNDATIONAL and INTERMEDIATE','carry','The best v1 measurement content: 56% (F) and 42% (I) directly observable; 88% of sampled competency-levels contain at least one direct non-proxy statement. Carry as raw material for L1-L2 indicators, adding conditions, standards and evidence metadata per indicator_writing_rules.md.','E','IO-010','IO'),
('Advanced indicators','Proficiency Indicators, level ADVANCED','change','Only 15% directly observable and 69% need specification; 21% opportunity-dependent (lead programs, manage portfolios); 17% compound. Rewrite to L3/L4 with explicit complexity and scope conditions.','E','IO-010','IO'),
('Expert-level statements (K, A and indicators)','Proficiency Indicators, level EXPERT','retire','61.4% not individually assessable; 22% proxies (publishes, recognized); 39% opportunity-dependent; on average 81% of each competency Expert statements match a few boilerplate frames. Only 1 of 43 sampled competencies has a direct non-proxy Expert statement. Do not migrate. Write new L4/L5 indicators only where the work exists.','E','IO-010','IO'),
('Publication, recognition and award indicators ("Publishes influential research", "Achieves recognition", "Recognized expert")','Proficiency Indicators, mainly EXPERT (publishes in 158 competencies; recognition in 103)','retire','Criterion-contaminated proxies that favor academic and well-resourced roles and are scored by others opinions; unusable for selection in agencies; adverse-impact and opportunity-access risk. A published method may serve as an evidence source for a performance indicator, never as the indicator.','E','IO-010|IO-020','IO'),
('Credential and training completion as indicators (e.g., 4.4.4 "Completes OSHA HAZWOPER Technician (40-hour) training")','4.4.4 all levels; scattered elsewhere','change','Credentials are qualification gates attached to positions, not levels of competence. 4.4.4 also appears to pair emergency-response levels (Awareness, Operations, Technician) with site-worker course hours (24 h, 40 h), which IO judges a content error (FC/CP to verify against 29 CFR 1910.120).','J','IO-010','IO'),
('Tool- and vendor-named indicators (ArcGIS, QuickBooks, Workiva, FARSITE, Tableau, blockchain, digital twin as the competency)','Indicators across D2, D3, D4','change','5.8% of sampled statements tool-locked (9% at Advanced); 17.9% of job tasks name AI or a specific technology. Move tools to the separately versioned tool layer and name the function in the indicator (DC lane).','E','IO-010','IO'),
('Job tasks (3 per competency; 666)','Competencies sheet Job Task 1-3; data/v1_baseline/tasks.csv','change','Verb-led (good) and close to O*NET task style, but: only 7.5% state a standard or protocol; 31% are compound; 8% lead with "Use" (tool-as-task); three tasks per competency is far too few for job analysis; tasks were written top-down from competencies rather than derived from jobs; about 76% of D3 task text was inferred (task sequence v7). Carry as seed items for the job-analysis survey task inventory, to be confirmed by incumbent ratings.','E','IO-010|IO-005|IO-044','IO'),
('Claim that T1-T3 run from foundational to advanced','TEAM_BRIEF summary; task order','retire','Not supported by v1 own tags: only 89 of 222 T1 tasks are tagged primary-learning (P); 170 of 222 T3 tasks are tagged contributing (C), only 11 specialist (X). Task position does not encode proficiency; level must come from the indicator model.','E','IO-002','IO'),
('Domain 5 proficiency indicators','Proficiency Indicators rows for 5.x.x (120 levels)','add','Parse defect in all database versions: K/A sit in the Indicator 1-2 columns with "Knowledge*:" and "Application*:" prefixes; Indicator 3 is the placeholder "Indicators*:"; zero real indicators for 30 competencies. The source text holds 706 D5 indicators. Recover them (DE), then rewrite to v2 rules. D5 scored lowest in the sample (6% direct, 50% usable) because only K/A could be rated.','E','IO-001|IO-002','IO'),
('Indicator truncation at import (6 per level cap)','data/v1_baseline/proficiency.csv qa_flag indicators_at_import_cap_6 (684 levels); source_text/indicators.csv','add','2,104 of 6,484 source-text indicators (32%) are absent from the database, including all 706 D5 indicators. Recover before rewriting so v2 does not lose usable observable content (DE lane).','E','IO-002','IO'),
('Competency descriptions merged into titles (19 competencies, e.g., 1.4.2, 3.1.4, 4.3.3)','Competencies sheet Description blank; title holds description','change','Data defect (DE). Matters for measurement because SMEs rate titles and definitions in Delphi and surveys; merged text confuses item stimuli.','E','IO-001|IO-002','IO'),
('Near-duplicate competencies (1.4.2 Wildlife survey techniques vs 4.1.2 Wildlife observation and sign interpretation)','Competencies 1.4.2, 4.1.2','change','Identical Foundational Application text ("Conducts wildlife surveys following (established) protocols") and overlapping indicators. Duplicates undermine discriminant validity and double-count in profiles. Merge or separate on a defined boundary (e.g., field detection vs survey design); CA to run a systematic near-duplicate screen.','E','IO-001','IO'),
('AI/robotics exposure instrument (5 dimensions on 666 tasks: automation type, tacit density, career-ladder position, vector, horizon)','Dimension Tags T13 columns; data/v1_baseline/tasks.csv; domain4_task12_working_record.md','needs-evidence','Concept sound and task-level grain correct, but codes come from a single analyst with an LLM, with no inter-rater reliability. v1 explicitly decided IRR provisions were not needed. The only repeated coding is same-rater version drift on D6 (auto type 95%, tacit 93%, career 89% agreement), which is consistency, not reliability. "Calibration" in v1 meant tuning the instrument to the analyst judgment. Run the s.7 gold-set study before any exposure statistic is published as more than analyst judgment.','E','IO-001|IO-002|IO-007|IO-009','IO'),
('Career Ladder Destruction (CLD) flag and severity','Dimension Tags T13: CLD Flag, CLD Severity','change','Deterministic rule (TRUE if any P-position Ac/S/V task) is violated in 11/222 competencies (5%): 7 D2 reconstructed rows should be TRUE, 3 D4 rows should be FALSE, and 4.1.3 should be TRUE. Severity uses out-of-dictionary values ("Highest", "Ungraded"); flags mix True/False/Yes/No/Y/N. Make CLD computed rather than stored (CA s.4) and validate inputs; keep the construct, which is important.','E','IO-001|IO-002','IO'),
('Craft primary/secondary tags','Dimension Tags Craft Primary/Secondary','needs-evidence','Single-rater irreducibility judgments; v1 own record lists many contested boundary cases (2.3.2 drone, LCA producer vs consumer, 7.2.3). Reliability unknown at competency or task level. Run the craft-weight pilot (validation_protocol.md s.7.3) before DP-5.','E','IO-006|IO-009','IO'),
('Workflow stage tags S1-S6','Dimension Tags Stage columns','needs-evidence','Single-rater; S1 holds 107 of 215 primary tags and S6 only 3, which may reflect coder convention rather than work. Test with the s.7.1 gold set and SME review; CA may generalize to work functions.','E','IO-001','IO'),
('Profession family Core/Supporting assignments (F1-F15)','Dimension Tags F1-F15; Profession Family View','change','Analyst-assigned importance. Replace with empirical importance and frequency from the job-analysis survey (validation_protocol.md s.4) aggregated by role profile; keep v1 values as priors only.','J','IO-001|IO-044','IO'),
('Ethical lens columns L1-L5','Dimension Tags L1-L5 (populated for 4 of 222)','needs-evidence','E/I/A coding is highly inferential (v1 reports ~95% of ethical content Implicit), so reliability is likely low without a strong codebook; transposed L2/L3 numbering across working documents adds error risk. If retained, run the s.7.1 reliability test before population; otherwise express ethics through observable indicators (e.g., 7.1.3 exemplar).','J','IO-001','IO'),
('Stability tier (Stable/Transition/Emergent)','Dimension Tags Stability Tier','carry','Derived rule applied consistently (0 violations against reform flags and Ac/S tasks), but it inherits the unvalidated inputs. Carry as a computed field once inputs are validated.','E','IO-001','IO'),
('Planned Delphi design (~30 panelists; 3-5 reviewers per competency; Tasks 20-21)','taxonomy_task_sequence_v7.md (Tasks 20-21); Delphi panel-composition prompt in project conversation record (~30 panelists, 3-5 reviewers per competency)','change','With 5 reviewers per item, CVR significance requires 5/5 essential; with 3 it is unattainable. No pre-registered thresholds, stopping rules or composition caps; SAF-led recruitment risks forestry skew. Replace with 15-25 per panel, pre-registered rules, CREDES/ACCORD reporting and contraction-bias correction (validation_protocol.md s.3, s.5).','E','IO-005|IO-008|IO-065|IO-066|IO-062|IO-063|IO-003','IO'),
('Sentinel network: single analyst with AI coding, no IRR','Infrastructure architecture decision conversation (2026-03-03); Structural Conditions report','change','Keep the sentinel idea (an annual leading indicator) but replace single-analyst coding with the s.7.2 LLM-plus-human protocol and composition caps. v1 itself identified the failure mode (AI resolves ambiguity silently) and the composition risk (contraction over-represents private datacraft practitioners).','E','IO-009|IO-003','IO'),
('Sector application notes (5 per competency)','Competencies sheet Public Agencies ... Academia','carry','Useful descriptive context; not assessable and should not be used in selection. Carry as context examples; CA may restructure as sector-actor variants.','J','IO-001','IO'),
('Domain 7 cross-cutting competencies (7.1.1-7.2.3)','Competencies 7.1.x, 7.2.x','carry','Most observable Foundational and Intermediate content in v1 (D7 sample: 40% direct), with explicit validation behaviors that suit assisted-mode assessment. Expert levels repeat the boilerplate and must be rewritten. 7.1.3 integrity needs care in selection use (SJT and work products only; never trait scoring).','E','IO-010','IO'),
('Hard-coded regulatory references in tasks and indicators (e.g., SEC climate disclosure in 3.6.2 T2; "NEPA scientific integrity requirements" in 7.1.3)','3.6.2, 7.1.3 and others','change','Rules change (2025 shifts in SEC climate disclosure and NEPA implementation, as IO understands them; unverified, SC/PS to confirm). Standards in indicators should reference applicable jurisdiction requirements via a jurisdiction overlay (jurisdiction_variable flag).','J','IO-010','IO'),
('v1 methodology recommendation of SFIA-style responsibility levels and level spans','Skills Taxonomy Architecture and Methodology...md (Proficiency scaling comparisons)','carry','v1 own research recommended a responsibility-first architecture that avoids forcing every skill into every level for mobility and career-pathway products. v2 adopts it (proficiency_model_v2.md).','E','IO-004|IO-061','IO'),
('Domain 5 stakeholder framing listing Tribes as a stakeholder category (5.2.1 source text Foundational indicator)','source_text/indicators.csv 5.2.1 foundational','change','Tribal nations engage as sovereign governments through consultation, not as stakeholders. Exemplar rewrite adds an indicator distinguishing the two; TN to review.','J','IO-002','IO'),
]
